From 1b7f61115560db2b6fdbc33e5d80ea7425c27cfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aibing Chen <chenaibing@cmss.chinamobile.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:14:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ieee802154: hwsim: fix double free when deleting a radio
 during a scan

hwsim_del() frees phy->pib before ieee802154_unregister_hw().
Unregistering the hardware closes the slave interface, which aborts an
ongoing scan and calls back into hwsim_hw_channel() and
hwsim_update_pib().  That installs a new PIB and schedules the old one
for kfree_rcu(), so the kfree_rcu() in hwsim_del() later frees the same
object a second time:

  BUG: KASAN: invalid-free in kvfree_call_rcu
   ...
   hwsim_update_pib
   hwsim_hw_channel
   ...
   hwsim_del

Free the PIB after the hardware has been unregistered, re-reading
phy->pib under pib_lock so that a PIB installed during teardown is freed
exactly once.

Fixes: 979d5b8de8ed ("ieee802154: hwsim: serialize pib updates to fix double-free")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: syzbot+8a8482d4c33cc58babb4@syzkaller.appspotmail.com
Closes: https://syzkaller.appspot.com/bug?extid=8a8482d4c33cc58babb4
Signed-off-by: Aibing Chen <chenaibing@cmss.chinamobile.com>
---
 drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c b/drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c
index a9bd1555d..004934d7c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c
@@ -1008,12 +1008,24 @@ static void hwsim_del(struct hwsim_phy *phy)
 		list_del_rcu(&e->list);
 		hwsim_free_edge(e);
 	}
-	pib = rcu_dereference(phy->pib);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 
-	kfree_rcu(pib, rcu);
-
 	ieee802154_unregister_hw(phy->hw);
+
+	/*
+	 * Unregistering the hardware closes the slave interface, which aborts
+	 * an ongoing scan and calls back into hwsim_hw_channel().  That
+	 * replaces phy->pib, so re-read the pointer here and free the PIB that
+	 * is current after teardown exactly once, instead of double-freeing
+	 * the one sampled before unregistering.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_bh(&phy->pib_lock);
+	pib = rcu_replace_pointer(phy->pib, NULL,
+				  lockdep_is_held(&phy->pib_lock));
+	spin_unlock_bh(&phy->pib_lock);
+	if (pib)
+		kfree_rcu(pib, rcu);
+
 	ieee802154_free_hw(phy->hw);
 }
 
